[{:db/id "q-37685/selection/05a0058bbc8b441c1868e3d9814e48f9cd21cf658b56b00b3123b8c12693c6c0" :answer/id #uuid "f80c770c-bcc9-5f93-a3e3-948113c20170" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37685/selection/27ac3dfbd95e351f0e2fd1ba3b1f6d9477175b36085c68ec2382205e0558c225" :answer/id #uuid "68f8b43f-8af8-50e1-b275-c7306bf5b0bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37685/selection/1f6d1ed3b8cc348c3b4283e4c82d59f49b9f2f3b41ae0b0cae2afd579084cbb0" :answer/id #uuid "f1d195e6-e0ea-5864-8b8d-4ad59c0ebc8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37685/selection/a8b0a41d6b5b964f4540fd5ee1b12eeecdae59b2e277a6339e3d97c16af77a7d" :answer/id #uuid "dcb4a4e1-8d2e-5332-b9fa-45abd01cf471" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37685/selection/6bb5bd51e88ab4c2f0a254bb49f7796492919213e4b821945711b6ff4776924d" :answer/id #uuid "deab1e46-423d-5377-a7db-718db1f3ec89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37685/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b23e53b-7f93-5056-a771-c9d32a10fe9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37685/selection/a8b0a41d6b5b964f4540fd5ee1b12eeecdae59b2e277a6339e3d97c16af77a7d" :answer-field/choices ["q-37685/selection/05a0058bbc8b441c1868e3d9814e48f9cd21cf658b56b00b3123b8c12693c6c0" "q-37685/selection/27ac3dfbd95e351f0e2fd1ba3b1f6d9477175b36085c68ec2382205e0558c225" "q-37685/selection/1f6d1ed3b8cc348c3b4283e4c82d59f49b9f2f3b41ae0b0cae2afd579084cbb0" "q-37685/selection/a8b0a41d6b5b964f4540fd5ee1b12eeecdae59b2e277a6339e3d97c16af77a7d" "q-37685/selection/6bb5bd51e88ab4c2f0a254bb49f7796492919213e4b821945711b6ff4776924d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37685" :question/id #uuid "699935ac-2009-58b3-9525-0eee26e7f93b" :question/math-academy-id "q-37685" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{y}^{1}dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}[x]_{y}^{1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}(1-y)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{y}{1+{y}^{2}})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{y}{1+{y}^{2}})\\,dy & ={[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{2})}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{1}^{2})}{2}-(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{0}^{2})}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-37685/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdce40e5-8ffe-52cb-8a8e-ac8eaea982f0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37685"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-37995"] :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}[x]_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}({y}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dy & ={[-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-40581/selection/23a46cc37d2b34990e02f1410bfddd251d76c663b3f2cacabc9958a5531f8931" :answer/id #uuid "68663c41-cbad-5a48-b049-d0c2c6b87c29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{-y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40581/selection/226fb4c61e40ef9695715aac0b06fdf9266ac44d07e36a3f57c70c12287f800e" :answer/id #uuid "a6743543-f257-5acb-be74-a00c26cc37d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y-2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40581/selection/116c65cd31fb154fd3cfe990e1e2ecc3fcc8871cc9475f0bad10bf48dcc3c480" :answer/id #uuid "6991940d-1769-5e65-9d9b-a0829ca8976d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40581/selection/f285b8487280321e0d253e893db060f4f171544230280ed6ce4bf413efc7ea22" :answer/id #uuid "4d43ead1-5851-518c-bb70-e7d98fa8f824" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40581/selection/97529c667ac96fe1cf6dbfc9e307881f22672d76b33e2af15f30ce2d653e8e8b" :answer/id #uuid "039a27b0-c098-58df-bad1-04addc11b577" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{-y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40581/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d5b1079-3494-53a8-b6e9-5cb48aa9323e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40581/selection/116c65cd31fb154fd3cfe990e1e2ecc3fcc8871cc9475f0bad10bf48dcc3c480" :answer-field/choices ["q-40581/selection/23a46cc37d2b34990e02f1410bfddd251d76c663b3f2cacabc9958a5531f8931" "q-40581/selection/226fb4c61e40ef9695715aac0b06fdf9266ac44d07e36a3f57c70c12287f800e" "q-40581/selection/116c65cd31fb154fd3cfe990e1e2ecc3fcc8871cc9475f0bad10bf48dcc3c480" "q-40581/selection/f285b8487280321e0d253e893db060f4f171544230280ed6ce4bf413efc7ea22" "q-40581/selection/97529c667ac96fe1cf6dbfc9e307881f22672d76b33e2af15f30ce2d653e8e8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40581" :question/id #uuid "362fcf20-6d09-5e57-8338-b11857a062d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-40581" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed between the curves $y=x-2,$ and $y=\\sqrt{x},$ above the $x$-axis. What is ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA\\,$ expressed as a repeated integral?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/assets/6817e13f2f4c019f337425bd9f2284386c7077c0ac97da51fc26fdea19f8ee67.png)\n\nWe need to represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=x-2$ and $y=\\sqrt{x}$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=x-2 & \\,⟹\\,x=y+2 \\\\ y=\\sqrt{x} & \\,⟹\\,x={y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =y+2 \\\\ {y}^{2}-y-2 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)(y+1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the $x$-axis the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/assets/db9d1846b19b75a629ad0a0d4b6e138aa2cef91cd8c0324a9285ed9c44befb60.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le y+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-40581/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ccbe70d-24f4-5e9c-8536-9ccab99f571b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40581"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132529/selection/9412ec94881d480f1cd6dfe3aa3ed25db7e09a8d11af1148913673a24947a173" :answer/id #uuid "791b381d-0c08-5c83-81ef-983fd6187469" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132529/selection/c49bfb7506c4ffc4d18e47b7ca75e9215b8d32ed8584ef76a3555cc2844cd31b" :answer/id #uuid "f147fce4-7d29-558a-8458-ba7e7ea536e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{4}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132529/selection/798daf07bea97d10f099818ed1dbabcea723307abba317cdbcf5469a3f8ba31d" :answer/id #uuid "58bbe423-9a00-5f5b-a460-1b71dc97d41c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{8}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132529/selection/8fe09e45f3c04354b99662812b8b171d4b2e66c194ea29df05975653c53b0b34" :answer/id #uuid "d5c12d64-7969-5e82-a624-258c1adab26b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132529/selection/4a9ab52ff1f7cde216cb2e7e8326e7144628cdf07909eb2747e37fc13f383f5c" :answer/id #uuid "0ba4d452-09ce-5907-9a59-c3ebde4b6bad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{4}+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132529/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "be3eee5a-bd68-599e-be5e-bf211f2309c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132529/selection/9412ec94881d480f1cd6dfe3aa3ed25db7e09a8d11af1148913673a24947a173" :answer-field/choices ["q-132529/selection/9412ec94881d480f1cd6dfe3aa3ed25db7e09a8d11af1148913673a24947a173" "q-132529/selection/c49bfb7506c4ffc4d18e47b7ca75e9215b8d32ed8584ef76a3555cc2844cd31b" "q-132529/selection/798daf07bea97d10f099818ed1dbabcea723307abba317cdbcf5469a3f8ba31d" "q-132529/selection/8fe09e45f3c04354b99662812b8b171d4b2e66c194ea29df05975653c53b0b34" "q-132529/selection/4a9ab52ff1f7cde216cb2e7e8326e7144628cdf07909eb2747e37fc13f383f5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132529" :question/id #uuid "d5f009be-0871-5507-bce4-956000cf9505" :question/math-academy-id "q-132529" :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{D}x{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dA,$ where $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,-y\\le x\\le 2y}.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,-y\\le x\\le 2y}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-y}^{2y}x{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-y}^{2y}x{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}[{\\int }_{-y}^{2y}x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{-y}^{2y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}(2{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dy & =\\frac{1}{2}{[{e}^{{y}^{3}}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132529/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90f7718f-e014-5232-acb1-6773ab79f61d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132529"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132563/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "19a872e1-08f8-5352-a1b6-d44f10bed845" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132563/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer/id #uuid "43ed516f-e22e-55e6-ad32-b94c7c7e22b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132563/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "0273b340-18ee-5c3c-bf39-48af0b32763c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132563/selection/4ca7e04cb32d17c1971e27f96c827d785e809ee86fbe2e04813f39f29bdc8cde" :answer/id #uuid "c6086d76-32de-51ed-bd89-d80000f6b1a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132563/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" :answer/id #uuid "f11f6044-a28f-5ff6-9cbe-f5e82f2b8b16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132563/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "494e7700-d265-5332-b3ff-cc8e557a559d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132563/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" :answer-field/choices ["q-132563/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-132563/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" "q-132563/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" "q-132563/selection/4ca7e04cb32d17c1971e27f96c827d785e809ee86fbe2e04813f39f29bdc8cde" "q-132563/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132563" :question/id #uuid "0d937870-20e3-5ed3-ad6f-56e0cffb3636" :question/math-academy-id "q-132563" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/assets/e15621dd6402a86de5c5d172880c7cbdc2a933e852259ad81d5ebcf9a89b9984.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}2x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=10$ and $y=2x+1,$ above the line $y=1,$ as shown in the picture." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x\\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=10 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}} \\\\ y=2x+1 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(y-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(y-1) \\\\ 2\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}} & =y-1 \\\\ (2\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}})^{2} & =(y-1)^{2} \\\\ 40-4{y}^{2} & ={y}^{2}-2y+1 \\\\ 5{y}^{2}-2y-39 & =0 \\\\ (5y+13)(y-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the line $y=1$, the $y$-limits are \n$1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/assets/33487fff6ff0b0e74bab4e6d6acdcb6902d40e938525d7de92d684ed5d98273a.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}(y-1)\\le x\\le \\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}2x\\,dA={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{(y-1)/2}^{\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}2x\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{(y-1)/2}^{\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}2x\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{(y-1)/2}^{\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}2x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[{x}^{2}]_{(y-1)/2}^{\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(10-{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}(y-1)^{2})dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(10-{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}(y-1)^{2})dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(10-{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}(y-1)^{2})dy & ={[10y-\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{12}(y-1)^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(30-9-\\frac{2}{3})-(10-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{61}{3}-\\frac{29}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132563/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90f7718f-e014-5232-acb1-6773ab79f61d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132563"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
